2
00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:08.880
<b>Grand Line
Momoiro Island (Kamabakka Kingdom)</b>

3
00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:13.780
What is this place?

4
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.490
And more importantly...

5
00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.620
What is with these guys!?

6
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.300
Damn it...

7
00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:45.060
Dear Nami-san, Robin-chan...

8
00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.090
Are you doing well?

9
00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:50.360
I can't wait to see you again.

10
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.570
When I do, I'm sure we'll become great friends.

11
00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:23.830
grow, grow and grow much stronger! (Yeah!)

12
00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:15.980
<b>The Underwater Prison Impel Down</b>

13
00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:25.810
I wanted you and Luffy to become great marines...

14
00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:32.100
Nevermind marines, you two brothers have become notorious outlaws.

15
00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:35.750
I'm sure you've heard the rumors about Luffy, too.

16
00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:39.580
In Water 7, he picked a fight with the World Government...

17
00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:43.750
and somehow managed to invade the Judicial Island, Enies Lobby.

18
00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:54.160
Oh, yeah. I also told Luffy about his father.

19
00:03:57.310 --> 00:04:01.370
He was really surprised to hear he had a father.

20
00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:04.050
Doesn't matter...

21
00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.110
Whether we know about it or not...

22
00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:07.950
as annoying as it is,

23
00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:12.480
both me and Luffy carry the blood of a world-renowned criminal.

24
00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.650
There's no way we could have ever been marines.

25
00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:21.320
Even though I owe my mother a debt of gratitude and took the name "Portgas"...

26
00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:25.810
I still can't stand the thought that I carry the blood of that worthless father of mine.

27
00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:29.890
I don't remember him at all, and I don't owe him anything.

28
00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:34.960
Yeah, I get what you mean, but he was just...

29
00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:34.960
That's why...

30
00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.000
Gramps...

31
00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:45.850
I'd hate to see you die right now, kid.

32
00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:54.350
Take my name and roam wild and free over the seas!

33
00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:56.790
Become my son!

34
00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:03.940
My old man is...

35
00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.870
Whitebeard, and no one else.

36
00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.480
Vice Admiral Momonga!

37
00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:21.010
We've spotted a pirate ship.

38
00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:22.930
Whose ship is it?

39
00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:26.360
I know I've seen that mark before...

40
00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:27.770
I'll go look into it right away!

41
00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:29.970
If you can't remember it offhand,

42
00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:32.310
then it can't be anyone important.

43
00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:33.820
Just ignore it.

44
00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:36.710
We must get to our destination quickly.

45
00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:37.650
Yessir!

46
00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:44.240
There's one! A giant Sea-King!

47
00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:48.620
If that thing spots us, it'll swallow the ship whole!

48
00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:52.310
Please don't look this way...

49
00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:56.130
It's gone.

50
00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:59.590
W-We've gotten this far...

51
00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:02.530
but I don't know what good we can do if we continue!

52
00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:07.600
What should we do now, Big Sis Alvida?

53
00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:10.390
Don't look at me.

54
00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:14.210
You were the ones who wanted to come here, right?

55
00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:17.570
You spent so much money on that Eternal Pose, too.

56
00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:24.250
Well, we have to save Captain Buggy, who was taken to Impel Down!

57
00:06:27.230 --> 00:06:28.660
Take a look at the sea.

58
00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:30.930
The Calm Belt lies just beyond here.

59
00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:32.670
That's the monsters' nest.

60
00:06:32.670 --> 00:06:35.590
Do you really think we can make it through with this ship?

61
00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:41.260
The only other route would be to go there on a Navy ship.

62
00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:45.970
The Gates of Justice won't open for a pirate ship, after all.

63
00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:49.360
No way! You mean we can't even get there?

64
00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:53.470
At this rate, Captain Buggy will be put to death!

65
00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:57.470
Along with our new buddy, Ace-kun!

66
00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:06.310
Impel Down is the world's largest prison, which can neither be broken into nor escaped from.

67
00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:10.370
You should just give up already.

68
00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:14.170
This just means that Buggy the Clown's luck as a pirate has run out.

69
00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:17.030
That's not true!

70
00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:21.430
Captain Buggy wouldn't bite the dust from something like this!

71
00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:24.720
He's right! We've sworn to keep following Captain Buggy...

72
00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:28.100
until the day when we finally find what we've been looking for:

73
00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:31.510
Captain John's treasure island!

74
00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:37.880
Richie!

75
00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:39.930
Do whatever you want, then.

76
00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:43.720
I'll take the Big Top, here.

77
00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:45.990
You guys can set off in a rowboat.

78
00:07:47.140 --> 00:07:50.410
No way! This is Captain Buggy's ship!

79
00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:54.330
Buggy isn't here, is he?!

80
00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:56.830
Yeah. You're right...

81
00:07:57.630 --> 00:08:01.650
I know if we go there, we'll all die, so I'm not going.

82
00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:03.710
It'd be a waste to bring the ship there, too.

83
00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:09.300
You guys can just chase after Buggy in a rowboat until you're satisfied.

84
00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:12.270
Yeah!

85
00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:16.600
Well, you'll probably die long before you even see Impel Down.

86
00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:24.030
Captain Buggy! Thank you so much for everything!

87
00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:27.660
We will never forget what you have done for us!

88
00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:31.390
We'll pray that your execution be quick and painless!

89
00:08:31.390 --> 00:08:32.870
Farewell!

90
00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:35.390
Let's meet again in the next life!

91
00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:41.230
This is Momonga.

92
00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:44.130
Marine code G-1 00660.

93
00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:46.000
I will enter the current shortly.

94
00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.590
Prepare to open the gates!

95
00:08:47.090 --> 00:08:58.520
<b>Current
location</b>
<b>Mariejois</b>
<b>Navy Headquarters
(Marineford)</b>
<b>Sabaody Archipelago</b>
<b>Enies Lobby</b>
<b>Amazon Lily</b>
<b>The Great Prison
Impel Down</b>

96
00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:51.350
The ship carrying Luffy and Hancock...

97
00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:54.350
is about to enter the current
connecting the three main facilities...

98
00:08:54.350 --> 00:08:55.840
of the World Government...

99
00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:58.520
the Tarai Current, which can only be used by the Navy.

100
00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:04.900
<b>Great Underwater Prison Impel Down</b>

101
00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:22.710
Please, kill me!

102
00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:27.090
Hey! Newbie!

103
00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:29.550
Why are you just sitting there,

104
00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:33.550
munching away at your bread without first greeting the boss of this cell?

105
00:09:34.770 --> 00:09:40.420
It's a rule around here that newbies are supposed to offer their food to the boss!

106
00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:52.810
Learned your lesson yet?

107
00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:17.340
Hey! Wait!

108
00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:19.380
We were just having a small fight!

109
00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:21.720
We ain't on death row!

110
00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:22.600
Let us out!

111
00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:55.110
Four and a half days have passed...

112
00:10:55.110 --> 00:10:58.470
since the departure from
 the Island of Women, Amazon Lily.

113
00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:03.900
Vice Admiral Momonga!

114
00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:07.090
The headwind slowed us down a little,

115
00:11:07.090 --> 00:11:09.830
but we've finally reached Impel Down!

116
00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:13.900
This is bad... We have to hurry.

117
00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:15.970
Get Hancock, now!

118
00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:16.950
Yessir!

119
00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:19.620
Hancock-dono! We have arrived!

120
00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:20.820
I will be there shortly.

121
00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:22.400
What's this?

122
00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:25.040
There are more warships here than there were in the Buster Call!

123
00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:29.500
Currently, this is the most dangerous place in the world.

124
00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:31.600
It is obvious that it would be well-guarded.

125
00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:35.340
So, Ace is inside here?

126
00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:38.950
He is probably far below the surface.

127
00:11:38.950 --> 00:11:41.180
Now, hide under my clothes.

128
00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:49.190
Welcome, Vice Admiral Momonga!

129
00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:59.030
L-Look at that!

130
00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:01.050
That's the Pirate Empress!

131
00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:02.790
She's more beautiful than anyone else!

132
00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:05.330
There's no limit to her beauty!

133
00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:09.990
How high can her Beauty Power rise? Ten thousand watts? A million?

134
00:12:11.650 --> 00:12:13.860
What is all the fuss about?

135
00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:15.810
Such a noisy bunch.

136
00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:17.290
May I petrify them?

137
00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:20.050
Please don't.

138
00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:24.130
The Navy doesn't need any more humiliation.

139
00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:28.540
Your condition for helping us was that you wanted to see the man at the center of these events,

140
00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:31.770
Portgas D. Ace, for yourself, right?

141
00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:33.330
I told you before,

142
00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:37.320
but this place is usually strictly off-limits for pirates, even the Seven Warlords of the Sea.

143
00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:40.510
Once you enter,

144
00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:42.970
you will be restrained with Seastone shackles.

145
00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:47.660
You will also have to go through a full body check at the entrance.

146
00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:53.730
We cannot let you free any of the inmates or anything, after all.

147
00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:58.090
Luffy. They will do a body check once we enter.

148
00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:00.920
We'll figure something out. Just keep going!

149
00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:04.930
I do not mind.

150
00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:06.360
What?

151
00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:07.800
Buggy the Clown?!

152
00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:09.350
He's escaped from his cell?!

153
00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:10.690
Is he a Devil Fruit User?

154
00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:13.780
Assistant Warden.

155
00:13:13.780 --> 00:13:18.230
Vice Admiral Momonga and the Warlord Hancock-dono have arrived.

156
00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:20.110
Right. I'll be there in a minute.

157
00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:25.360
She's so cu...uh...open the gates!

158
00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:28.410
Give her whatever service she wants!

159
00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:34.330
Time left until Ace's execution...

160
00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:37.670
33 hours.

161
00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:42.460
Here we go, Luffy.

162
00:13:46.710 --> 00:13:48.270
Do take care!

163
00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:52.390
Hancock-sama! Have a safe trip!

164
00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:53.810
Stop your buzzing, little flies!

165
00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:57.190
Don't be cruel! Take care, now!

166
00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:05.620
Help us!

167
00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:07.700
Help!

168
00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:10.370
What an oppressive atmosphere.

169
00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:12.920
Is this what hell is like?

170
00:14:13.630 --> 00:14:15.300
We have finally made it inside.

171
00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:17.880
We cannot relax yet, however.

172
00:14:20.470 --> 00:14:24.340
I welcome you to my Impel Down!

173
00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:26.320
Ah! My mistake!

174
00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:29.410
Calling it "my" Impel Down is too ambitious!

175
00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:32.610
I am still but the assistant warden, Hannyabal!

176
00:14:32.610 --> 00:14:35.000
Pleasure to meet you!

177
00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:36.900
I'm Momonga.

178
00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:38.780
I've heard what you're here for.

179
00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:42.170
And you must be the Empress, Hancock-dono?

180
00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:45.320
My Empress, Hancock-dono?

181
00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:46.800
Oh, forgive me!

182
00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:48.370
I'm being too ambitious again!

183
00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:50.080
That stinking warden...

184
00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:52.080
Oh! My mistake.

185
00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:57.270
Warden Magellan is in his office down in Level 4.

186
00:14:57.270 --> 00:14:59.620
You will be taken there right now.

187
00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:04.550
Your escorts will be Vice Chief Jailer Domino here, and myself.

188
00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:07.670
It seems you are short on time, so please, come this way.

189
00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:12.140
Vice Admiral, you go over there and undergo your body check.

190
00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:19.730
Our prisoners are all sent into this cage where they are stripped of their clothes...

191
00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:24.790
...and lowered into pots of boiling water.
We call this process the "Lukewarm Bath of Hell".

192
00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:29.330
We use it to "disinfect" and baptize our prisoners, before they are put in their cells.

193
00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:33.020
Even among those prisoners, there are some who are tougher than others.

194
00:15:33.020 --> 00:15:37.080
A few of our recent inmates, Fire Fist Ace...

195
00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:40.500
as well as the Warlord Jinbe, and...

196
00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:43.590
the former Warlord, Crocodile...

197
00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:48.600
...all went through the baptism
without even batting an eyelash.

198
00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:54.700
Here you are.

199
00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:57.060
Guests check in inside this private room.

200
00:15:57.060 --> 00:15:58.290
Don't worry.

201
00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:09.030
Please remove that cloak.

202
00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:12.530
It's the easiest way to conceal someone,

203
00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:14.460
so please hand it over to me.

204
00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:17.550
I have no reason to suspect you,

205
00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:20.150
but if you were thinking of pulling anything suspicious,

206
00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:26.050
we have monitoring Transponder Snails all over Impel Down.

207
00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:29.970
They transmit everything they see to the security monitors.

208
00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:35.980
Well then, first things first.

209
00:16:36.530 --> 00:16:38.830
Put on these Seastone shackles.

210
00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:42.630
I am not even a prisoner, yet I still need shackles...

211
00:16:42.630 --> 00:16:44.490
You are too cautious.

212
00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:51.740
Please, be gentle with me.

213
00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:57.040
What?

214
00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:03.170
You can come out now, Luffy.

215
00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.220
That was close!

216
00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:13.180
I thought I'd have to make a break for it when they weren't watching...

217
00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:16.060
You can turn anything into stone, huh?

218
00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:20.520
This seems to be as far as I can take you.

219
00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:24.310
After this, my abilities will be restrained by Seastone.

220
00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:26.860
And you won't be able to hide once they've taken my cloak.

221
00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:31.210
I had hoped to be of more help to you...

222
00:17:31.210 --> 00:17:32.880
What're you saying?

223
00:17:32.880 --> 00:17:36.410
There's no way I'd have made it all the way here by myself!

224
00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:39.960
You got me inside a building surrounded by warships.

225
00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:41.380
You've helped me plenty!

226
00:17:42.510 --> 00:17:43.790
Luffy...

227
00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:49.530
This is a stronghold made to lock people away.

228
00:17:49.530 --> 00:17:52.940
No matter what happens, please do not cause an uproar here.

229
00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:56.590
If you get captured, you will never be able to get out.

230
00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:04.570
Though you are strong, will you promise me to not cause any disturbances?

231
00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:08.910
Right, I got it! I promise!

232
00:18:08.910 --> 00:18:10.780
Thanks a lot, Hancock!

233
00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:13.990
I'll never forget what you did for me!

234
00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:15.700
I'll definitely repay you someday!

235
00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:18.500
Just now... you...

236
00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:20.360
called me...

237
00:18:20.360 --> 00:18:22.970
Hancock?!

238
00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:26.750
Sure thing, Hammock!

239
00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:28.960
Hammock, I want more food!

240
00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:31.050
What's up, Hammock?

241
00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:36.490
Hancock!

242
00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:49.110
Now my life is complete!

243
00:18:51.700 --> 00:18:53.910
Hey, you can turn them back now.

244
00:18:53.910 --> 00:18:55.120
I'll be fine!

245
00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:59.490
This must be... a mutual affection!

246
00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:01.160
They sure are taking their time...

247
00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:05.530
It's a security check, so we have to be thorough about it.

248
00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:09.350
Even those parts...?!

249
00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:12.220
What are you imagining?

250
00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:16.010
Assistant Warden Hannyabal!

251
00:19:16.010 --> 00:19:19.790
The surveillance Transponder Snail isn't transmitting anything...

252
00:19:19.790 --> 00:19:21.350
Is everything all right in there?

253
00:19:23.940 --> 00:19:26.650
Domino! Is something wrong?

254
00:19:33.350 --> 00:19:35.320
The body-check is complete.

255
00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:40.290
The surveillance is working again. No problems.

256
00:19:40.290 --> 00:19:42.050
I am so sorry.

257
00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:43.620
Did that take too long?

258
00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:46.000
Not at all!

259
00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:47.540
No problems here either.

260
00:19:48.590 --> 00:19:52.360
What tasteless treatment of someone who isn't a prisoner...

261
00:19:52.360 --> 00:19:54.520
Just who do you think I am?

262
00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:55.960
Please tolerate it.

263
00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:59.640
It's one of the rules of Impel Down.

264
00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:01.130
This is strange...

265
00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:03.390
My memory feels hazy...

266
00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:05.270
Please lead the way.

267
00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:09.310
As you wish. Head toward the mega-lift over there.

268
00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:15.030
Using this lift, we'll go down to the fourth undersea floor.

269
00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:20.130
That will take us to the Inferno, where Prison Warden Magellan's office is.

270
00:20:20.130 --> 00:20:22.730
I should warn you, it's pretty hot down there.

271
00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:28.630
Luffy?!

272
00:20:30.550 --> 00:20:32.100
I will pray for your fortune.

273
00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:35.760
(Thank you!)

274
00:20:37.310 --> 00:20:39.470
He said "I love you"!

275
00:20:41.180 --> 00:20:42.140
Hey!

276
00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:44.620
H-Hancock-dono! What's wrong?

277
00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:45.560
Be careful with her.

278
00:20:45.560 --> 00:20:48.100
What's this all of a sudden?

279
00:20:56.210 --> 00:20:58.650
Well, now where do I go?

280
00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:01.570
That lift is going down,

281
00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:05.320
and Hancock said Ace was probably at the bottom of the sea...

282
00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:06.650
That's it!

283
00:21:06.650 --> 00:21:08.540
This is what I've got the Vivre Card for.

284
00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:33.190
The Blugori jailers are coming back.

285
00:21:33.190 --> 00:21:35.080
They've secured food.

286
00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:36.230
Open the hatches.

287
00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:41.710
Good job.

288
00:21:41.710 --> 00:21:43.860
Carry the meat to the freezers.

289
00:21:47.250 --> 00:21:48.910
We've found him!

290
00:21:48.910 --> 00:21:52.830
The escaped pirate from Shared Cell 4
in Level 1, Buggy the Clown!

291
00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:55.300
We've confirmed that he's standing in the hall by Isolation Cell 22!

292
00:21:55.300 --> 00:21:57.080
Capture him immediately!

293
00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:59.220
Damn, they found me, huh?

294
00:21:59.220 --> 00:22:01.430
You bastards!

295
00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:07.520
We've lost contact with
 surveillance Transponder Snail #71!

296
00:22:07.520 --> 00:22:09.560
Did you hear that? It's Buggy!

297
00:22:09.560 --> 00:22:13.540
Serves him right for trying to escape on his own!

298
00:22:13.540 --> 00:22:16.230
He's got a horrible punishment waiting for him!

299
00:22:19.240 --> 00:22:20.990
There they are! The Blugori!

300
00:22:20.990 --> 00:22:22.410
Go!

301
00:22:22.410 --> 00:22:23.910
Go get him!

302
00:22:29.710 --> 00:22:32.370
The Vivre Card is telling me to go down here, but...

303
00:22:32.370 --> 00:22:34.570
It's a dead end, huh?

304
00:22:39.570 --> 00:22:42.050
Prisoner number 8200.

305
00:22:42.050 --> 00:22:44.010
What? We're not letting him get away!

306
00:22:45.800 --> 00:22:47.910
They've verified him as a Devil Fruit user!

307
00:22:47.910 --> 00:22:49.610
Don't forget the Seastone!

308
00:22:51.770 --> 00:22:52.650
Hurry!

309
00:22:53.190 --> 00:22:54.910
We'll split up and surround him!

310
00:22:58.690 --> 00:22:59.900
Right! I'm in!

311
00:22:59.900 --> 00:23:01.130
Hurry!

312
00:23:02.810 --> 00:23:04.200
What's that?

313
00:23:04.190 --> 00:23:08.560
<b>Level 1 - Crimson Floor</b>

314
00:23:10.420 --> 00:23:12.250
Are all these rooms prison cells?

315
00:23:14.940 --> 00:23:15.970
Screams?

316
00:23:15.970 --> 00:23:18.250
Well, whatever. Anyway, I've gotta keep going!

317
00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:22.710
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

318
00:23:22.710 --> 00:23:23.790
Huh?

319
00:23:23.800 --> 00:23:25.680
Bro! Bro!

320
00:23:25.680 --> 00:23:26.550
What?

321
00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:28.070
Wait a sec!

322
00:23:28.070 --> 00:23:30.360
What're you doing outside the cage?

323
00:23:30.360 --> 00:23:31.980
Huh? What's up?

324
00:23:31.980 --> 00:23:35.310
Outside the cage? I came from the outside...

325
00:23:35.310 --> 00:23:36.220
See ya!

326
00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:39.060
Wait! Don't lie, dammit!

327
00:23:39.060 --> 00:23:40.790
I ain't lying!

328
00:23:40.790 --> 00:23:42.290
Who are you?

329
00:23:42.290 --> 00:23:44.810
You're not a jailer or a torturer, are you?

330
00:23:44.810 --> 00:23:47.660
How come you're outside the cage?!

331
00:23:47.660 --> 00:23:50.490
You sure are noisy!

332
00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:52.660
Oh, right! Do you guys know where Ace is?

333
00:23:52.660 --> 00:23:54.490
Ace?

334
00:23:54.490 --> 00:23:57.880
Ace... you mean...

335
00:23:58.990 --> 00:24:00.960
Fire Fist Ace?

336
00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:03.670
That's right. I wanna save Ace!

337
00:24:04.800 --> 00:24:06.470
Don't be so reckless!

338
00:24:06.470 --> 00:24:10.180
True, I did hear that he'd been sent here...

339
00:24:10.180 --> 00:24:13.450
If he is, then he's probably down in Level 5!

340
00:24:13.450 --> 00:24:15.160
No way you'd be able to get near that place.

341
00:24:15.160 --> 00:24:15.980
It's impossible!

342
00:24:15.980 --> 00:24:21.240
That's where they keep the guys with bounties over a 100 million, ya know!

343
00:24:22.440 --> 00:24:24.240
Level 5?

344
00:24:24.240 --> 00:24:25.680
Anyway, Bro.

345
00:24:25.680 --> 00:24:29.680
Mind going to the jailers' room and stealing the keys?

346
00:24:30.340 --> 00:24:32.660
Yeah! Please, Bro!

347
00:24:32.660 --> 00:24:39.460
Don't you think that it must have been fate that we met here, in this huge world?

348
00:24:43.680 --> 00:24:45.130
What's that?

349
00:24:45.720 --> 00:24:47.050
The Blugori!

350
00:24:47.050 --> 00:24:48.270
Blugori?

351
00:24:48.270 --> 00:24:49.580
Run away, Bro!

352
00:24:49.580 --> 00:24:50.680
They'll kill ya!

353
00:25:00.860 --> 00:25:02.820
What's with these guys?!

354
00:25:02.820 --> 00:25:05.280
To the right!

355
00:25:05.280 --> 00:25:07.450
To the left!

356
00:25:11.410 --> 00:25:13.030
Fools!

357
00:25:13.030 --> 00:25:15.790
Don't look down on the man with the power of the Split-Split Fruit!

358
00:25:19.760 --> 00:25:21.580
Straw Hat?!

359
00:25:21.580 --> 00:25:23.910
Why are you here?!

360
00:25:25.600 --> 00:25:27.500
Oh. Buggy, huh?

361
00:25:27.500 --> 00:25:30.970
Why you... don't screw with me, you lowlife!

362
00:25:30.970 --> 00:25:33.220
You're as cheeky as ever, I see!

363
00:25:33.220 --> 00:25:36.560
I didn't know you were captured, too!

364
00:25:36.560 --> 00:25:39.130
I came here on my own!

365
00:25:39.130 --> 00:25:40.860
I wasn't captured!

366
00:25:41.650 --> 00:25:44.480
What sort of idiot would willingly enter a prison?

367
00:25:45.320 --> 00:25:49.070
Wait, could it be that you heard of my imprisonment...

368
00:25:49.070 --> 00:25:51.940
and came to rescue me?

369
00:25:51.940 --> 00:25:53.490
Like hell!

370
00:25:53.490 --> 00:25:56.490
–Dumbass! I'm getting sick just thinking about it.

371
00:25:55.160 --> 00:25:57.860
–What the hell are you talking about?!

372
00:25:58.160 --> 00:26:01.920
I promised Hancock that I wouldn't cause an uproar here,

373
00:26:01.920 --> 00:26:03.420
but you got me dragged into this!

374
00:26:03.420 --> 00:26:05.750
It's not like I wanted you to get involved!

375
00:26:13.960 --> 00:26:20.060
Well, I just got foiled in
"Buggy's Great Jail-Break Plan"!

376
00:26:20.060 --> 00:26:21.790
Who gives a damn?!

377
00:26:24.400 --> 00:26:26.320
They're coming from the front, too!

378
00:26:26.320 --> 00:26:28.280
Damn it!

379
00:26:28.280 --> 00:26:30.570
Hey! Why are you escaping, anyway?

380
00:26:30.570 --> 00:26:33.490
What're you talkin' about, stupid?!

381
00:26:33.490 --> 00:26:36.830
You don't know the kinds of torture they put me through!

382
00:26:36.830 --> 00:26:40.070
These guys are cold-blooded monsters!

383
00:26:40.070 --> 00:26:42.040
Then you just have to avoid getting caught, right?

384
00:26:42.040 --> 00:26:43.880
W-W-What are you talking about?!

385
00:26:43.880 --> 00:26:45.710
I'm in a hurry!

386
00:26:45.710 --> 00:26:48.920
Come to think of it, I guess I've already caused an uproar.

387
00:26:51.170 --> 00:26:55.050
That's the thing I can't stand about you and that Red-Hair...

388
00:26:55.050 --> 00:26:59.410
You're always thinking positively, but in a bad way.

389
00:27:02.890 --> 00:27:05.950
Fine. Let's do this!

390
00:27:05.950 --> 00:27:07.820
We'll just have to do it, won't we?!

391
00:27:10.230 --> 00:27:11.780
Time for a great, flashy...

392
00:27:13.910 --> 00:27:16.030
change of plans!

393
00:27:16.030 --> 00:27:17.900
Agreed!
